-- title:
--   Characteristic 2 supersingular places: 12 |W| = ψ(M')
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and suppose there is a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$. Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$, and let $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ \kappa\ M'$ be the intermediate field of the Laurent series field over $\kappa$ generated by the $j$-series `jqModC` and its $M'$-fold substitute `jqNModC`. Places of this field over $\kappa$ are, by definition, valuation subrings that contain the image of $\kappa$, are proper, and are principal ideal rings. Let $W$ be a finite set of such places whose members are exactly the elements of $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\ q\ M'\ \kappa$, that is, exactly those places $w$ that are rational, satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ at the generator `jGeomGen` lies in the set $\mathrm{ssJSet}\ q\ \kappa$ of supersingular $j$-invariants. The conclusion is the identity of natural numbers
--   $$12 \cdot |W| = \mathrm{dedekindPsi}\ M' = \sum_{d \mid M',\ d \text{ squarefree}} M'/d.$$
--
--   This is the closed form, under the stated congruence condition on a prime divisor of the level, of the Eichler–Deuring mass formula counting supersingular points on $X_0(M')$ in characteristic $2$: the automorphism group of the unique supersingular curve acts with trivial stabilisers on the $\psi(M')$ cyclic subgroups of order $M'$, so that the number of supersingular points is $\psi(M')/12$. It is used in the computation of the genus of the reduction of the full-level modular curve at $2$ via the supersingular charts.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_twelve_mul_card_eq_dedekindPsi_of_ssPlaces_of_eq_two_of_dvd.lean

